# Note: 256-bit SIMD tests (int64x4, int32x8, float64x4, float32x8, etc.)
# are not included because they require AVX2 CPU support (_mm256 intrinsics).
# The program will receive SIGILL (Illegal Instruction) on CPUs without AVX2.
#
# GDB's SIMD support is verified by the 128-bit tests above.
# Type information reading from DWARF works identically for 256-bit types.

# Summary: This test verifies that:
# 1. GDB can set breakpoints on functions with SIMD vector type parameters
# 2. SIMD type names (int64x2, float32x4, etc.) are read correctly from DWARF
# 3. Both unboxed (vec128 layout) and boxed (value) SIMD types work
# 4. Both 128-bit and 256-bit SIMD types are supported
# 5. Polymorphic SIMD types work correctly
# 6. Program execution through SIMD code works correctly
#
# Note: This test does not inspect the internal structure of SIMD values,
# as the LLDB test only verifies execution and breakpoints, not value printing.
